{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/feedback.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-15T04:35:19.109547Z","id":"b55c6e805a1370f7acda105967914d58f46ea5f0b7d0aadd04fc68020507edf7","body":{"detail":"Withhold::approval runs Store::request_state once per thread that withholds anything, so a listing of N such threads makes N indexed reads (plus st.owner() when the owner is withheld). Versions and names are cached per call. vis_threads_ms (Task 25) will show whether it matters.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":1516},"end":{"line":1543},"content_hash":"3010c690f14394938e54d31bb2735f0d0f34d547f7848a1ec64b159faa9b7fe8"},"summary":"Each thread with withheld content costs one approval_requests query in a listing","supersedes":"7667d7a0a57b0940668680afc4230d0cef6073d4aebe277f0b58093fedaf27c9","tags":["perf","visibility","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/feedback.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-15T04:35:19.111025Z","id":"e06baf6365d21a100539cb5fa229539fac9bd59b74d762bc3031d9ac60bbdb4e","body":{"detail":"Spec §8.3 gives a thread withheld: {count, authors, approval} whenever any field is withheld but does not say what count counts. Withhold::thread counts withheld comments (the number the feedback line and approval requests speak of), so a thread whose only withheld field is its anchor, clip, resolved_by or a batch note has count 0.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":1566},"end":{"line":1610},"content_hash":"472a63a615cac43e0ca525689a793d0aab4ecaadecaaef4ad8767556155767a4"},"summary":"A thread's withheld.count counts its withheld comment bodies only","supersedes":"fecb18e9e8aa2b9130cff8d8414119f565a32fbe4abfc71d09f49e77357d8b30","tags":["visibility","spec:8.3","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/feedback.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-15T05:10:36.214470Z","id":"e1ac7b33ee4a9d1cea9b7ad15a404166fe57429e6b5f5862f244c1d2cc68266d","body":{"detail":"Withhold::approval runs Store::request_state once per thread that withholds anything, so a listing of N such threads makes N indexed reads (plus st.owner() when the owner is withheld). Versions and names are cached per call. vis_threads_ms (Task 25) will show whether it matters.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":1470},"end":{"line":1497},"content_hash":"3010c690f14394938e54d31bb2735f0d0f34d547f7848a1ec64b159faa9b7fe8"},"summary":"Each thread with withheld content costs one approval_requests query in a listing","supersedes":"b55c6e805a1370f7acda105967914d58f46ea5f0b7d0aadd04fc68020507edf7","tags":["perf","visibility","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/feedback.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-15T05:10:36.216036Z","id":"be9e166b760b3d2f6208452a24711c43922fd0ba9fc7cfd5693ff6d0d32ea1a6","body":{"detail":"Spec §8.3 gives a thread withheld: {count, authors, approval} whenever any field is withheld but does not say what count counts. Withhold::thread counts withheld comments (the number the feedback line and approval requests speak of), so a thread whose only withheld field is its anchor, clip, resolved_by or a batch note has count 0.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":1520},"end":{"line":1564},"content_hash":"472a63a615cac43e0ca525689a793d0aab4ecaadecaaef4ad8767556155767a4"},"summary":"A thread's withheld.count counts its withheld comment bodies only","supersedes":"e06baf6365d21a100539cb5fa229539fac9bd59b74d762bc3031d9ac60bbdb4e","tags":["visibility","spec:8.3","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/feedback.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-15T05:59:02.534101Z","id":"1cdecf55a81cabfde4abbd6a1bdef570999d3026a34991033d43db8db5aa7406","body":{"detail":"Store::register_session_restoring returns the note (spec 2026-10-08 §6.7) and FeedbackWaiters::set_note keeps it in a map until the session's first feedback poll; nothing in the database records it. The watches are restored either way; only the note is lost.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":79},"end":{"line":86},"content_hash":"4d34e0a7296ea8660cd602c9300047b0e20c46410bd0aec30d2f7a513618e2e6"},"summary":"A restored session's note is kept in daemon memory, so a daemon restart before its first poll drops it","supersedes":"7cba5514a453d4b465d89b59e4853e4108ddc681d6e30a4f8aba438d5f94726c","tags":["revisit:a session column or table for one-shot notes","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/feedback.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-15T05:59:02.536069Z","id":"4a9df0127daf1afc479e16d046b29fb526841f29df179557c5db033817136f53","body":{"detail":"Spec §8.3 gives a thread withheld: {count, authors, approval} whenever any field is withheld but does not say what count counts. Withhold::thread counts withheld comments (the number the feedback line and approval requests speak of), so a thread whose only withheld field is its anchor, clip, resolved_by or a batch note has count 0.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":1521},"end":{"line":1565},"content_hash":"472a63a615cac43e0ca525689a793d0aab4ecaadecaaef4ad8767556155767a4"},"summary":"A thread's withheld.count counts its withheld comment bodies only","supersedes":"be9e166b760b3d2f6208452a24711c43922fd0ba9fc7cfd5693ff6d0d32ea1a6","tags":["visibility","spec:8.3","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/feedback.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-15T05:59:02.574561Z","id":"987a59eb77518fe04b50101b6d83aae41cf84077e638d5b407f03303450f10bb","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:09672011","summary":"Measured: scripts/perf-daemon.sh at 09672011 times GET /api/artifacts/<id>/threads as a person's agent on 200 comments by four authors over 20 threads, each withholding another author's comments: median 2.17 ms over three rounds (3.23, 1.79, 2.17) against vis_threads_ms's limit of 2.84 ms (baseline 0.84 ms at d17ba57b plus 2 ms); quick runs 2.35 and 2.79 ms; minimum 1.3 to 1.5 ms. The per-thread request_state reads fit the budget.","supersedes":"e1ac7b33ee4a9d1cea9b7ad15a404166fe57429e6b5f5862f244c1d2cc68266d","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
